{"parentUuid":"2fb32e7c-2876-4e5d-b071-21d7edcf1909","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01FuSCETdKaMQqUSkgWjcxA4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Here's what was wrong and what I changed.\n\n## Root cause\nBoth 3D graphs in the Bridge — the Documents knowledge graph and Code 3D — render through `three_renderer` ([index.js](prime-silo/app/L0/_all/mod/_prime_silo/widgets/three_renderer/index.js)), which wraps `3d-force-graph`. It created the scene, fed it data, and stopped there. It **never framed the camera**. `3d-force-graph` parks the camera at a fixed default distance, so any graph bigger than that default extends past the frustum and spills off the edge — exactly the right-side overflow in your Code 3D screenshot. There was also no canvas resize handling, so split/Expand layout changes left the canvas clipped.\n\n## Fix (in `three_renderer/index.js`)\n- **Frame-to-fit on settle:** registers `onEngineStop` → calls `zoomToFit(600ms, 60px)` once the force layout cools, so the whole graph lands in view.\n- **Re-fit on data change:** a `needsFit` flag re-frames after each `graphData` update (ingest, filter toggles) but *not* on idle re-settles — so it won't fight your manual pan/zoom.\n- **Resize tracking:** a `ResizeObserver` keeps the WebGL canvas sized to its host and re-fits on panel/Expand/split changes (the lib only listens for window resizes otherwise).\n- All new calls are guarded (`typeof … === \"function\"`), and new behavior is opt-out via `fitOnLoad`/`fitPaddingPx`/`fitDurationMs`.\n\nBoth 3D paths benefit — `bridge.js` routes the docs KG ([:864](prime-silo/app/L0/_all/mod/_prime_silo/bridge/bridge.js:864)) and code graph ([:1253](prime-silo/app/L0/_all/mod/_prime_silo/bridge/bridge.js:1253)) through `makeThreeRenderer` → `createThreeRenderer`.\n\n## Tests\nAdded three cases to [widgets_three_renderer_test.mjs](prime-silo/tests/widgets_three_renderer_test.mjs) (fit on engine stop, re-fit after update, fit-disabled skips registration). Full suite passes.\n\n**One caveat on verification:** this is an Electron shell widget that loads `3d-force-graph` from a CDN at runtime and needs the Benny backend — I can't drive it in a browser preview from here, so I verified at the unit level rather than visually. To confirm the camera framing live, launch the desktop app, open Code 3D, and toggle to 3D — the graph should now center and fit instead of running off-frame. If you want, I can run the devops `run`/build skill to launch it.\n\nThe 2D \"Classic Benny\" renderer is a separate vendored path; your report was specifically about 3D, so I left it untouched — say the word if 2D also overflows for you."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1483,"cache_read_input_tokens":87183,"output_tokens":1218,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1483,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1218,"cache_read_input_tokens":87183,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1483,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1483},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CcUYNX5Wiqps2nY1Szp7i","type":"assistant","uuid":"17108cd4-2c84-4a18-9b8f-29cb6d4bf7e4","timestamp":"2026-06-27T22:19:47.336Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\prime-silo","sessionId":"1231aaa9-d9f4-4d01-9820-86f32a823a60","version":"2.1.187","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
