{"parentUuid":"c1746569-e850-4fee-814d-dbcb751bd616","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01QavVsAPaGoW8CzyGLJBgcJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both suites pass. Here's the second round of fixes.\n\n## What was wrong\nTwo separate renderers, two separate gaps:\n\n**3D (`three_renderer`) — no labels + tight.** It only ever set node color/size. It never rendered any text, and it left `3d-force-graph`'s default forces (weak charge ≈ −30, short links), which pack nodes into unreadable clumps. Default physics mode is `fluid` for both graphs ([bridge.js:375,380](prime-silo/app/L0/_all/mod/_prime_silo/bridge/bridge.js:375)), so the 3D scene runs its own simulation — which is exactly where weak repulsion bites.\n\n**2D (`force_graph_2d`) — names overlap.** It *does* draw labels, but it also never tuned repulsion, so dense clusters collided.\n\n## Changes\nIn [three_renderer/index.js](prime-silo/app/L0/_all/mod/_prime_silo/widgets/three_renderer/index.js):\n- **Floating 3D labels** via the optional `three-spritetext` module, lazy-loaded from its own CDN and attached with `nodeThreeObjectExtend(true)` (keeps the colored sphere, adds the name beside it). Best-effort — if the sprite CDN is blocked, the scene still renders.\n- **Hover tooltip** (`nodeLabel`) showing friendly name + full identifier — works even without the sprite module.\n- **Spacing:** stronger charge (−120) and longer links (45) via `d3Force`, so clusters open up.\n- Shared `labelFor`/`identifierFor` helpers mirror the 2D renderer's naming priority (kg3d `display_name`, codegraph path→basename, memory `content`), so a File reads `auth.py` not `/src/app/auth.py`.\n\nIn [force_graph_2d/index.js](prime-silo/app/L0/_all/mod/_prime_silo/widgets/force_graph_2d/index.js):\n- Same `d3Force` spacing (charge −180, links 60) so the 2D labels stop overlapping.\n\nAll knobs are option-overridable (`showLabels`, `chargeStrength`, `linkDistance`, `labelColor`, …) and every lib call is guarded, so the test stubs (which lack these methods) stay green. Added 5 new 3D tests (labels, force tuning, label-disabled path) and both suites pass.\n\n**Caveat, same as before:** these are Electron shell widgets that load their graph libs from a CDN and need the Benny runtime — I verified at the unit level, not visually, since I can't drive the desktop app from here. To confirm live: open Code 3D in 3D mode — you should now see names floating by each node and looser, readable clusters. One thing to watch: persistent labels on a very large code graph can get busy; if it's too noisy, we can switch 3D to hover-only labels or label only larger nodes — tell me which you'd prefer after you see it."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":226,"cache_read_input_tokens":120854,"output_tokens":1850,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":226,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1850,"cache_read_input_tokens":120854,"cache_creation_input_tokens":226,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":226},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CcUYp9ePPjf3yDDgBxCKw","type":"assistant","uuid":"413705cc-ec00-4161-ac72-8ac59d4bfb4f","timestamp":"2026-06-27T22:25:44.080Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\prime-silo","sessionId":"1231aaa9-d9f4-4d01-9820-86f32a823a60","version":"2.1.187","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
